1
00:00:00,755 --> 00:00:03,579
Twenty-seven days of selfies, one answer:

2
00:00:03,579 --> 00:00:05,371
since starting this serum,

3
00:00:05,371 --> 00:00:08,195
redness is better and hydration is worse.

4
00:00:10,168 --> 00:00:11,014
That's Proof.

5
00:00:11,014 --> 00:00:14,792
It runs your skincare like a small trial on your own face,

6
00:00:14,792 --> 00:00:17,918
with YouCam Skin AI as the measuring instrument.

7
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:22,030
Why not just compare before and after?

8
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:25,658
Because skin scores wobble a few points between two photos taken

9
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:26,509
a minute apart.

10
00:00:26,509 --> 00:00:31,611
Track ten concerns and a product that does nothing still looks like it improved something,

11
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:32,575
most of the time.

12
00:00:34,541 --> 00:00:37,693
So you start by saying what the product claims to fix.

13
00:00:37,693 --> 00:00:41,021
That's your question, decided before you see any results.

14
00:00:42,823 --> 00:00:43,398
Day zero:

15
00:00:43,398 --> 00:00:45,253
three photos, a minute apart.

16
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:47,491
Your skin can't change in a minute,

17
00:00:47,491 --> 00:00:51,071
so any difference between YouCam's scores is pure noise,

18
00:00:51,071 --> 00:00:54,077
for your face, your phone, your bathroom light.

19
00:00:54,077 --> 00:00:57,146
Some concerns stay steady to a couple of points;

20
00:00:57,146 --> 00:01:00,343
others wobble more, so their verdicts take longer.

21
00:01:02,143 --> 00:01:03,962
Every few days you check in.

22
00:01:03,962 --> 00:01:07,016
One photo is noisy, so small changes stay grey.

23
00:01:07,016 --> 00:01:10,524
Until the last check-in you only see the trend so far:

24
00:01:10,524 --> 00:01:14,553
no verdict, because peeking every few days would let luck win.

25
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:20,528
At the final check-in, every concern gets a verdict with a range.

26
00:01:20,528 --> 00:01:22,630
'No real change' is a real answer:

27
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:25,474
the product isn't doing anything you'd notice.

28
00:01:25,474 --> 00:01:28,813
This demo trial was simulated with known true effects,

29
00:01:28,813 --> 00:01:31,100
and you can check Proof against them.

30
00:01:33,068 --> 00:01:36,775
I tested the method on two thousand simulated trials.

31
00:01:36,775 --> 00:01:38,873
When the product does nothing,

32
00:01:38,873 --> 00:01:43,209
a before-and-after selfie finds an improvement in 66% of them.

33
00:01:43,209 --> 00:01:43,629
Proof:

34
00:01:43,629 --> 00:01:44,258
under 5%.

35
00:01:44,258 --> 00:01:45,307
Under the hood:

36
00:01:45,307 --> 00:01:46,286
YouCam's file,

37
00:01:46,286 --> 00:01:51,042
task and polling APIs behind a small Node server that keeps the key,

38
00:01:51,042 --> 00:01:54,888
caps the units and deletes every task after reading it.

39
00:01:56,842 --> 00:01:59,451
At the end you get a card you can share,

40
00:01:59,451 --> 00:02:01,342
a review or a refund request,

41
00:02:01,342 --> 00:02:05,320
with a signature on every scan so nobody can quietly edit the

42
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:05,842
numbers.

43
00:02:07,802 --> 00:02:08,212
Proof.

44
00:02:08,212 --> 00:02:11,081
Stop guessing whether your skincare works.

